cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its outputs, please cite it as below."
title: "surrey-biome-pipeline: a two-extent test of scale-free climate downscaling against polygon-scale water stress"
abstract: >-
  Code, method and applied output for a controlled test of whether
  high-resolution "scale-free" downscaled climate data predicts polygon-scale
  vegetation water stress better than the same variables degraded to a coarse
  regional-model grid. Run at two extents: Surrey's 153 Green Infrastructure
  Network corridors, where the contrast was too small to test the question, and
  a 100 km Fraser Valley elevation transect, where the coarse model
  significantly outperformed the scale-free one. Also contains CDEI, a
  Sentinel-2 and Landsat index of polygon water stress, mapped and ranked
  across Surrey's corridors and validated against independent radar and climate
  data.
type: software
